# Environment Variables Template
# Copy this to .env.local and fill in your API keys

# Claude API (Recommended - Best reasoning)
# Get from: https://console.anthropic.com/api/keys
# Sign up free, create an API key, paste it here
VITE_CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-

# OpenAI API (Optional fallback)
# Get from: https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-

# Firebase Configuration (already set up, shown for reference)
# VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-key
# VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-domain
# etc...

# ==========================================
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS
# ==========================================

# 1. For Claude (RECOMMENDED):
#    a) Go to https://console.anthropic.com
#    b) Create account (free)
#    c) Go to API Keys
#    d) Click "Create Key"
#    e) Copy the key (starts with "sk-ant-")
#    f) Paste after "VITE_CLAUDE_API_KEY="
#    g) Save this file as ".env.local" in project root
#    h) Restart: npm run dev

# 2. For OpenAI (optional fallback):
#    a) Go to https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#    b) Create account or sign in
#    c) Generate API key
#    d) Paste after "VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY="
#    e) Restart: npm run dev

# 3. If you have both, Claude will be used (better reasoning)

# 4. If you have neither:
#    - App still works with rule-based responses
#    - Less detailed, but no cost
#    - Upgrade anytime by adding an API key

# ==========================================
# COST
# ==========================================

# Claude: ~$0.003 per question = 333 questions for $1
# OpenAI: ~$0.001-0.01 per question = 100-1000 questions for $1
# Fallback: Free (but less detailed)

# ==========================================
# TESTING
# ==========================================

# After setup:
# 1. npm run dev
# 2. Go to http://localhost:5174
# 3. Click "AI Chat" (sidebar)
# 4. Ask: "How is Area A?"
# 5. If you see detailed explanations -> SUCCESS!
#    If you see generic responses -> API key might be missing
